cases.prompt:
This function leaks when a caller reads one item, cancels ctx, and stops receiving. Assume calculate is synchronous and always returns promptly. Explain the cause and show a bounded fix preserving a streaming channel result.

func Stream(ctx context.Context, jobs []int) <-chan int {
    out := make(chan int)
    go func() {
        defer close(out)
        for _, job := range jobs { out <- calculate(job) }
    }()
    return out
}

Describe how a test could establish producer termination after cancellation without relying on an arbitrary sleep or resuming/draining the abandoned output.
